              "type": "text_file",
              "name": "Folder: GHOST -- Hospital Infrastructure Assessment",
              "takeable": true,
              "readable": true,
              "text": "GHOST -- HOSPITAL INFRASTRUCTURE ASSESSMENT (D. Foster)\n\nNetwork map of St. Catherine's Regional. Patient monitoring and critical care topology. FTP server flagged: ProFTPD, unpatched source build. Exploitation feasibility: HIGH.\n\nEmail, D. Foster to V. Sterling: \"Assessment complete. FTP vulnerability confirmed exploitable, architecture documented. Ready for the client. -DF\"\n\nSterling's reply, one line: \"Perfect. Security-awareness client, as discussed. Bill it to research.\"",
              "observations": "The reconnaissance that made St. Catherine's possible -- with Sterling's lie about the client sitting right underneath it.",
              "onRead": { "setVariable": { "danny_evidence_seen": true } }
            },
            {
              "type": "text_file",
              "name": "Personal notes (unsent)",
              "takeable": true,
              "readable": true,
              "text": "It was my map. My vulnerability notes. She said it was a security-awareness client.\n\nThen I saw the news. The ward. The topology matched exactly what I documented.\n\nI asked her. She said I was being paranoid, that hospitals get attacked all the time. Then she offered me a raise and called me 'essential'. She knows that I know.\n\nI should go to someone. But if I do, I'm the man who drew the map. What happens to them? To me?",
              "observations": "Danny's own notes to himself. Not sent to anyone."
            }
          ]
        }
